    "readme": "## Google Maps Scraper\n\nGoogle Maps Scraper automates Google Maps searches and user interactions to extract structured place and business data at scale. It locates places via search terms, categories, direct place URLs, or custom geolocation areas (polygons, multipolygons, point+radius), scrolls result lists, opens place pages and captures visible details. The Actor outputs rich place-level data including business name and address, geocoordinates, phone numbers and websites, company contact enrichment (emails, contact numbers, social links), leads enrichment (person names, job titles, LinkedIn/profile links, work emails when available), social profile enrichment (platform profiles and metrics), review data (review text, ratings, publish dates, owner responses, review images, per-service ratings and distributions), average ratings and review counts, opening hours, popular times histograms and live occupancy, images, menus, price brackets, booking/order links, hotel- and restaurant-specific metadata, indoor/multi-venue relations, and a variety of additional attributes and tags. Technical capabilities include simulating human interactions on Google Maps (search, scroll, enqueue place pages), flexible search scopes (free-text queries, categories, coordinates, custom GeoJSON areas), support for large-area scraping via tiled polygons or circles, and optional add-on enrichment modules for deeper contact and social profile data.\n\n## Use cases\n\n- Generate qualified leads by extracting business contact details, websites, and enriched contact profiles for prospecting.\n- Track competitors across regions by monitoring locations, ratings, and review counts.\n- Perform market analysis: assess market saturation, identify service gaps, and benchmark businesses by size, rating, and visibility.\n- Discover partnership opportunities by finding top-rated or high-volume locations for outreach.\n- Automate and scale local research workflows to replace manual Google M... [truncated]
